.SH DESCRIPTION
Smart Tree \- An intelligent directory visualization tool. Not just a tree, it\*(Aqs a smart\-tree!
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR
Specify input type explicitly (filesystem, qcp, sse, openapi, mem8)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Path to analyze (directory, file, URL, or stream)
.SH "GETTING STARTED"
.TP
\fB\-\-cheet\fR
Show the cheatsheet \- quick reference for all commands
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information and check for updates
.TP
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Generate shell completion scripts (bash, zsh, fish, powershell)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-man\fR
Generate the man page
.TP
\fB\-\-update\fR
Check for updates and install the latest version
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Skip the automatic update check on startup
.SH "DAEMON CONTROL"
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-update\fR
Install a stable release and restart the managed daemon (root, opt\-in service only)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
warn
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
debug
.IP \(bu 2
trace
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-start\fR
Start the Smart Tree daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-stop\fR
Stop the Smart Tree daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-status\fR
Show Smart Tree daemon status
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-context\fR
Get context from the daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-recall\fR \fI<RECALL>\fR
Recall indexed files and remembered context through the daemon (JSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-projects\fR
List projects tracked by the daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\-credits\fR
Show Foken credits from daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR
Bypass daemon and scan locally (standalone mode)
.SH "INTERACTIVE MODES"
.TP
\fB\-\-spicy\fR
Launch Spicy TUI \- interactive file browser with fuzzy search!
.TP
\fB\-\-terminal\fR
Launch Smart Tree Terminal Interface (STTI)
.TP
\fB\-\-dashboard\fR
Launch web dashboard (browser\-based terminal + file browser)
